      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nThe current implementation duplicates the `__atomic_compare_exchange_n` call and uses several \"magic numbers\" (`0xFFU`, `0xFF000000U`, `0x00FFFFFFU`, `0x00400000U`, `24`, `8`) inline. \n\nPlease extract these domain primitives into named constants and flatten the nested branches by combining the conditions for the atomic update. This eliminates the duplicated branch and ensures self-documenting code.\n\n```c\n#define TRACK_TAG_SHIFT 24\n#define TRACK_LO_SHIFT 8\n#define TRACK_TAG_MASK 0xFF000000U\n#define TRACK_LO_MASK 0x00FFFFFFU\n#define TRACK_ROLLOVER_THRESHOLD 0x00400000U\n\n/* ... inside get_time() ... */\n\t\t/* Lock-free timer overflow detection for b/213342294 */\n\t\tuint32_t cur_hi_tag \u003d (ts.le.hi \u003c\u003c TRACK_TAG_SHIFT) \u0026 TRACK_TAG_MASK;\n\t\tuint32_t cur_lo_val \u003d ts.le.lo \u003e\u003e TRACK_LO_SHIFT;\n\t\tuint32_t cur_packed \u003d cur_hi_tag | cur_lo_val;\n\n\t\tuint32_t prev_packed \u003d\n\t\t\t__atomic_load_n(\u0026track_packed, __ATOMIC_RELAXED);\n\t\tuint32_t prev_hi_tag \u003d prev_packed \u0026 TRACK_TAG_MASK;\n\t\tuint32_t prev_lo_val \u003d prev_packed \u0026 TRACK_LO_MASK;\n\n\t\tif (prev_hi_tag \u003d\u003d cur_hi_tag \u0026\u0026 prev_lo_val \u003e cur_lo_val \u0026\u0026\n\t\t    (prev_lo_val - cur_lo_val) \u003e TRACK_ROLLOVER_THRESHOLD) {\n\t\t\tts.le.hi++;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif ((prev_hi_tag \u003d\u003d cur_hi_tag \u0026\u0026 cur_lo_val \u003e prev_lo_val) ||\n\t\t    (int8_t)((cur_hi_tag - prev_hi_tag) \u003e\u003e TRACK_TAG_SHIFT) \u003e 0) {\n\t\t\t__atomic_compare_exchange_n(\u0026track_packed, \u0026prev_packed,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t    cur_packed, 0,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t    __ATOMIC_RELAXED,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t    __ATOMIC_RELAXED);\n\t\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/4404ef33-8178-4b25-9e17-96e783966b04)",
